    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Talking about music",
     "texto": [
      "People: **el cantante**, **el compositor**, **el músico**, **el guitarrista**, **el pianista**, **el director de orquesta**, **el bailarín**. Words in **-ista** are the same for men and women: **el / la** guitarrista.\n\nYou **tocar** an instrument (la guitarra, el piano, el violín, **la batería**). You **cantar**, **bailar**, **componer** and **ensayar**.\n\nA band **saca** an album, **da** a concert and **está de gira**. Music played during the concert is **en directo** (or **en vivo**).\n\nA song has **letra** and **música**. If many people like it, it is **un éxito**.\n\nTo say what music does to you, use the pattern of **gustar**: **me emociona**, **me relaja**, **me pone** in a good mood, **me recuerda a** my childhood.\n\n**Tener buen oído** is to notice sounds well. **Saberse** a song **de memoria** is knowing all of it."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Desde hace, instruments and «me emociona»",
     "texto": [
      "Three resources to talk about music:\n\n- **Desde hace** + time, with the present: something that began in the past and goes on now. **Toca la batería desde hace diez años.**\n- **Tocar** an instrument, **cantar** a song, **componer** music and **ensayar** before the concert.\n- Verbs like **gustar**: the thing is the subject and you go with **me / te / le**. **Esa canción me emociona. Esa canción me recuerda a mi infancia.**"
     ],
